<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tolistobogii</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tolistoboii</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tolistobogii were one of the three Celtic tribes of Galatia in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, alongside the Tectosages and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trocmi">Trocmi</a>. They crossed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> in 278 BCE and settled the western part of Galatia around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordion">Gordion</a> and Pessinus. Like the other tribes they were divided into four tetrarchies, and their tetrarch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deiotarus">Deiotarus</a> became king of all Galatia in the 1st century BCE.</p></div>
